  ],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"This has the supertype world. When a world permanent enters, any world permanents that were already on the battlefield are put into their owners' graveyards. This is a state-based action called the \"world rule.\" The new world permanent stays on the battlefield. If two world permanents enter at the same time, they're both put into their owners' graveyards.","oracle_id":"06eb8b90-aad8-41c1-bbc5-85ded2fe76bc","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It removes Flying from all creatures on the battlefield when it enters and from each creature as that creature enters. It does not prevent the Flying ability being given to the creature *after* the Sphere is on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"8ddf93fe-980b-4dc4-b56f-6a2ee50100a6","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This has the supertype world. When a world permanent enters, any world permanents that were already on the battlefield are put into their owners' graveyards. This is a state-based action called the \"world rule.\" The new world permanent stays on the battlefield. If two world permanents enter at the same time, they're both put into their owners' graveyards.","oracle_id":"8ddf93fe-980b-4dc4-b56f-6a2ee50100a6","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To work as an evasion ability, an attacking creature must already have flying when the declare blockers step begins. Once a creature has become blocked, giving it flying won’t change that.","oracle_id":"f7518456-45ed-41d4-bd3c-5aacea28eb35","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
